WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:06.340
Thanks to everyone who requested this video.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:09.250
Stick around to the end of this video if you
want to hear about how this movie first got

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:10.270
my attention.

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:13.910
A lot of people have been comparing this movie
to Groundhog Day, because they’re both about

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:17.780
someone reliving the same day over and over,
and there’s even a montage in Groundhog

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:21.790
Day where Bill Murray constantly tries to
kill himself to break the cycle, which the

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:24.920
girl in this movie… apparently her name
is Tree…

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.180
"Tree, Happy Birthday."

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.850
hold up who names their kid Tree?

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:33.050
Is it because she’s sprouting with new life
each day, is it cause she needs to become

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.510
one with nature, is it cause the killer is
constantly trying to cut her down?

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:38.970
OK, I’m done.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.480
But we see her trying to kill herself to get
out of the cycle too, and we see her just

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:47.250
experimenting, so there’s probably going
to be a lot of homage to Groundhog Day.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:52.710
Like the fact that she wakes up to the same
song every day.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:58.670
"Now put your little hand in mine..."

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.989
This shot’s got a ton of media references.

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:02.940
First up, a poster for They Live.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:07.450
It’s a movie about these glasses that allow
him to see the truth, that aliens have taken

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.030
over most positions of social importance.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:14.140
This is just speculation, but maybe tree finds
something that helps her see the truth about

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.140
who her killer is.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:18.361
I don’t really know anything about Adventure
Time, you can leave your interpretation in

00:01:18.361 --> 00:01:19.361
the comments.

00:01:19.361 --> 00:01:21.812
I think now is a good time to also mention
that not all of these things have to have

00:01:21.812 --> 00:01:23.050
some deep meaning to them.

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:27.229
It could just be that the character who’s
dorm this is likes Adventure Time, or Repo

00:01:27.229 --> 00:01:30.450
Man, so I’m not gonna dwell on these too
much until I’ve seen the movie.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:34.590
I will however point out that I thought this
was a Boston Bruins logo at first, it actually

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:38.010
might be the logo for the fictional college
that they go to: Bayfield University.

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:42.330
It also kind of conflicts with this thermos
that says Loyola University.

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:46.850
My theory is that’s where they filmed it,
Loyola University New Orleans, but they rebranded

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:50.520
it into Bayfield University for the purposes
of the plot.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:55.600
Here we see a flag for said Bayfield University,
and take note of the Baby graphic on the left.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:59.650
So it seems that the killer in this movie
is the school mascot, or at the very least,

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:01.630
someone who has access to the mascot costume.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:04.740
If you’re wondering where I got the rest
of the name of the school it’s right there

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:08.360
on a little card, and once you notice it,
the label is everywhere.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:12.319
So it seems they have a great sense of school
pride at this university.

00:02:12.319 --> 00:02:16.830
Tree lives at a Sorority house that starts
with Greek letter K, but seems to spend most

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:19.630
of her time with XEK fraternity.

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:23.840
In this scene, it looks like the object that
the killer breaks to stab her with is a actual

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:24.840
bong.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.130
I guess the killer is a part of vape naysh
y’all.

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:31.040
When she leaves Williams Hall, she’s approached
by this woman wearing a Tree Huggers United

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.260
shirt who asks her to stop global warming.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:35.170
"Stop global warming?"

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:39.319
So maybe all of those jokes I was saying earlier
about her name being Tree might actually be

00:02:39.319 --> 00:02:40.330
kind of relevant.

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:45.610
Perhaps the movie is an allegory for environmental
preservation with tree representing the environment

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:48.660
and her killer representing global warming
and pollution.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:52.350
She only has so much time to figure out the
mystery of who the killer is, just as we are

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:54.709
running out of time to save our environment.

00:02:54.709 --> 00:02:56.530
Birthday - Earth Day, I don’t know.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:57.530
Maybe there’s something there.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:01.459
Right after she wakes up screaming you can
see a poster of a comic woman screaming in

00:03:01.459 --> 00:03:02.459
the background.

00:03:02.459 --> 00:03:06.870
In this drowning scene, her hair is a different
color, this could be a test to see if physical

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.250
changes carry over to the next cycle.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:13.500
So the original title of this film was Half
To Death, which makes a lot less sense to

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:17.280
me than Happy Death Day, but when I heard
the name Happy Death Day, I was immediately

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:23.060
interested because one of my favorite Alien
Ant Farm songs shares the same title.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:24.819
"Happy Death Day to you!"

00:03:24.819 --> 00:03:28.360
It’s also kind of funny because not more
than a month ago, a movie called American

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:31.390
Made was released, which is also a Fall Out
Boy song.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:35.410
But anyway, I hope Happy Death Day the song
is in the credits or something when I see

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:36.410
the movie.

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:38.459
And on that note, the movie will be released
this Friday.

00:03:38.459 --> 00:03:43.250
I’m gonna try to have a video out by then,
so it should come a day early this week.

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:47.800
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors twice a week in October -- ring that

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:51.050
deathbell for notifications and I’ll see
you in the next one.

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:52.900
Assuming we both survive.

